{"l":8320,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The coach did not shout after the defeat. He simply asked each player to write down one thing they could have done better.' Hvad kendetegner trænerens reaktion?","o":["Han er skuffet og vil helst give op nu","Han er vred og vil straffe hele holdet","Han er rolig og vil have dem til at lære","Han er ligeglad med, hvordan det gik"],"a":"Han er rolig og vil have dem til at lære","r":"Han råber ikke, men beder spillerne om at tænke over, hvad de kan forbedre."},
{"l":8340,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Oliver's grandmother learned to use a tablet at 85. Now she sends the family photos every morning and corrects their spelling in the group chat.' Hvordan beskrives bedstemoren?","o":["Som træt og gammeldags","Som streng og vred","Som glemsom og forvirret","Som nysgerrig og aktiv"],"a":"Som nysgerrig og aktiv","r":"Hun lærte noget nyt som 85-årig og bruger det hver dag. Hun er nysgerrig og aktiv."},
{"l":8352,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'at blive færdig inden tiden' på engelsk?","o":["to beat the clock","to beat about the bush","to turn back the clock","to set the pace"],"a":"to beat the clock","r":"'to beat the clock' betyder at blive færdig inden tiden. Udtrykket betyder at nå noget, før tiden løber ud."},
{"l":8390,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Even the coach admitted that the other team had played better, although our team had won by one goal.' Hvad mener træneren?","o":["At de spillede bedst","At de var heldige at vinde","At kampen var kedelig","At dommeren tog fejl"],"a":"At de var heldige at vinde","r":"Træneren indrømmer, at modstanderne spillede bedre, selv om hans hold vandt."},
{"l":8420,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Sam always says he doesn't care about winning. Still, he was the last to leave training every day before the final.' Hvad antyder teksten om Sam?","o":["Han er ligeglad med finalen","Han kommer tit for sent","Han går meget op i at vinde","Han kan ikke lide at træne"],"a":"Han går meget op i at vinde","r":"'Still' viser en modsætning: han siger, han er ligeglad, men han træner mere end alle andre."},
{"l":8460,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The village has no shop, no school and only two buses a day. Yet most people who move there never want to leave.' Hvad er overraskende ved landsbyen?","o":["At landsbyen har mange busser","At der ligger en ny skole","At folk hurtigt flytter væk igen","At folk bliver boende trods manglerne"],"a":"At folk bliver boende trods manglerne","r":"'Yet' viser en kontrast: selv om der mangler meget, vil folk ikke flytte."},
{"l":8490,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The old cinema was going to be pulled down. After hundreds of local people wrote letters and organised events, the plans were changed.' Hvorfor blev planerne ændret?","o":["På grund af borgernes indsats","På grund af en ny ejer","På grund af dårligt vejr","På grund af mangel på penge"],"a":"På grund af borgernes indsats","r":"Hundredvis af lokale skrev breve og holdt arrangementer, og derefter blev planerne ændret."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'hvorved' på engelsk i 'He sold the house, ___ avoiding debt'?","o":["thereafter","thereby","whereas","hereby"],"a":"thereby","r":"'Thereby' = hvorved, på den måde."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'problem / spørgsmål' på engelsk i 'This is a serious ___'?","o":["tissue","invoice","issue","offer"],"a":"issue","r":"'Issue' betyder her et problem eller en sag."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'uvillige' på engelsk i 'The children were ___ to go home'?","o":["eager","allowed","excited","reluctant"],"a":"reluctant","r":"'Reluctant' = uvillig."},
{"l":8520,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'You had better ___ your bike, or someone might steal it.'","o":["lock","to lock","locked","locking"],"a":"lock","r":"'Had better' efterfølges af grundformen uden 'to': 'had better lock'."},
{"l":8540,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'commence' i 'commence the ceremony'?","o":["cancel","begin","attend","record"],"a":"begin","r":"'Commence' er et formelt ord for at begynde, altså 'begin'."},
{"l":8560,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'afskaffe' på engelsk?","o":["abandon","absorb","abolish","abstain"],"a":"abolish","r":"'Abolish' betyder afskaffe, fx en lov eller en regel. 'Abandon' betyder at forlade eller opgive."},
{"l":8570,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The organisers called the festival a modest success. Roughly half the tickets were sold, and it only rained twice.' Hvordan vurderer arrangørerne festivalen?","o":["Som en kæmpe succes for alle gæster","Som en total fiasko fra første dag","Som alt for dyr at gennemføre igen","Som nogenlunde, men ikke helt vellykket"],"a":"Som nogenlunde, men ikke helt vellykket","r":"'A modest success' betyder en beskeden succes; halvdelen af billetterne blev solgt, så det gik nogenlunde."},
{"l":8590,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'What I really need right now ___ a long holiday.'","o":["is","are","being","were"],"a":"is","r":"I en 'What'-kløvet sætning er 'What I really need' et ental-subjekt, så verbet er 'is'."},
{"l":8610,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'lethargic' i 'feel lethargic after lunch'?","o":["anxious","sluggish","cheerful","hungry"],"a":"sluggish","r":"'Lethargic' betyder sløv og uden energi, altså 'sluggish'."},
{"l":8640,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Is it going to rain at the weekend? I hope ___.'","o":["no","don't","not","none"],"a":"not","r":"'I hope not' erstatter en hel nægtende sætning (I hope it will not rain). 'I hope no' er forkert."},
{"l":8680,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'uundværlig' på engelsk?","o":["indisputable","indistinct","independent","indispensable"],"a":"indispensable","r":"'Indispensable' betyder uundværlig. 'Indisputable' betyder ubestridelig, og 'indistinct' betyder utydelig."},
{"l":8700,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'fordomsfri' på engelsk i 'Travelling abroad can make young people more ___.'?","o":["open-minded","absent-minded","single-minded","narrow-minded"],"a":"open-minded","r":"'Open-minded' betyder fordomsfri. 'Narrow-minded' er det modsatte, og 'absent-minded' betyder distræt."},
{"l":8720,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'meandered' i 'The river meandered slowly through the valley.'?","o":["styrtede","bugtede sig","tørrede ud","frøs til"],"a":"bugtede sig","r":"'Meander' betyder at bugte sig eller slynge sig langsomt, som en flod gennem et landskab."},
{"l":8740,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'I would rather you ___ my phone without asking.'","o":["don't use","won't use","didn't use","haven't used"],"a":"didn't use","r":"Efter 'would rather' + et andet subjekt bruges datid om nu eller fremtid: 'I would rather you didn't use'."},
{"l":8770,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'amateur' i 'an amateur photographer'?","o":["talented","young","keen","professional"],"a":"professional","r":"En 'amateur' gør noget som hobby, så det modsatte er en 'professional', der lever af det."},
{"l":8800,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The ferry is cancelled, so we ___ as well go home.'","o":["might","would","should","ought"],"a":"might","r":"'Might as well' betyder, at man lige så godt kan gøre noget, fordi der ikke er et bedre alternativ."},
{"l":8830,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'touch and go' i 'It was touch and go whether we would catch the last ferry.'?","o":["helt sikkert","meget usikkert","ganske ligegyldigt","meget dyrt"],"a":"meget usikkert","r":"'Touch and go' betyder, at udfaldet er meget usikkert, og at det kunne gå begge veje."},
{"l":8860,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'obscure' i 'an obscure band'?","o":["modern","unusual","famous","loud"],"a":"famous","r":"'Obscure' betyder ukendt, så det modsatte er 'famous' (berømt)."},
{"l":8900,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'She said she would finish the essay by Friday, and she ___.'","o":["made","was","got","did"],"a":"did","r":"'Did' erstatter hele udsagnet 'finished the essay by Friday' (substitution), så man undgår gentagelse."},
{"l":8940,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The museum is, admittedly, not the largest in the country, but what it lacks in size it more than makes up for in charm.' Hvad mener skribenten om museet?","o":["Lille, men meget charmerende","Stort, men lidt kedeligt","Hverken stort eller charmerende","Landets største og flotteste"],"a":"Lille, men meget charmerende","r":"'What it lacks in size it more than makes up for in charm' betyder, at charmen mere end opvejer den lille størrelse."},
{"l":8980,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man vil bede nogen om ikke at presse én til at beslutte sig hurtigt?","o":["Don't hurry on me.","Don't rush me.","Don't stress me up.","Don't push me over."],"a":"Don't rush me.","r":"'Don't rush me' betyder 'lad være med at skynde på mig'. 'Push me over' betyder at skubbe én omkuld."},
{"l":8996,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'altafgørende' på engelsk?","o":["tantamount","paranoid","paramount","peripheral"],"a":"paramount","r":"'Paramount' = vigtigst af alt."},
{"l":9008,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'afgørende / central' på engelsk?","o":["partial","pitiful","primal","pivotal"],"a":"pivotal","r":"'Pivotal' = helt central."},
{"l":9010,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'hindered' i 'The heavy backpack hindered his progress up the hill.'?","o":["hæmmede","hjalp","målte","viste"],"a":"hæmmede","r":"'Hinder' betyder at hæmme eller hindre; den tunge rygsæk gjorde det sværere at komme op."},
{"l":9020,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Scarcely ___ the house when it started to snow.'","o":["we had left","had we left","have we left","we have left"],"a":"had we left","r":"'Scarcely' først i sætningen kræver inversion, og mønstret er 'Scarcely had ... when ...' med førnutid."},
{"l":9031,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'naiv' på engelsk?","o":["native","noble","naive","vain"],"a":"naive","r":"'Naive' = naiv."},
{"l":9043,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'modvilje' på engelsk?","o":["relevance","reliance","resonance","reluctance"],"a":"reluctance","r":"'Reluctance' er navneordet til 'reluctant': modvilje."},
{"l":9050,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'disgruntled' i 'The disgruntled fans left the stadium before the final whistle.'?","o":["utilfredse","begejstrede","forvirrede","udmattede"],"a":"utilfredse","r":"'Disgruntled' betyder utilfreds eller sur; fansene gik før tid, fordi de var utilfredse."},
{"l":9054,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'godtroende' på engelsk?","o":["fallible","gullible","audible","legible"],"a":"gullible","r":"'Gullible' = let at narre."},
{"l":9060,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'anerkende' på engelsk i 'The school wants to ___ the hard work of its volunteers.'?","o":["acquaint","accumulate","acknowledge","accommodate"],"a":"acknowledge","r":"'Acknowledge' betyder at anerkende. 'Accumulate' betyder at samle sammen, og 'accommodate' betyder at give plads til."},
{"l":9066,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'uvurderlig (meget værdifuld)' på engelsk?","o":["invariable","inevitable","invisible","invaluable"],"a":"invaluable","r":"Pas på: 'invaluable' betyder meget værdifuld, ikke værdiløs. Værdiløs hedder 'worthless'."},
{"l":9077,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'stædig' på engelsk?","o":["obstinate","obsolete","obedient","fortunate"],"a":"obstinate","r":"'Obstinate' = stædig."},
